li.p:
for the Bymycar and Bilendi websites (Maximiles,
                            Meinungsplatz…), their multi-country FrontOffice/BackOffice are based on an
                            internationalized component-oriented PHP/Symfony architecture
                            (100 bundles);

Bymycar uses a microservices architecture: REST API for importing vehicles from the ERP into
                            the site, webhook for sending leads generated by the site into Salesforce, then sales
                            opportunities generated by Salesforce into a dealership sales solution…;

development of a PoC using the new Ballerina technology:
                                    a “data-centric” and “cloud-native” language targeting integration scenarios between
                                    applications, microservice architectures and data processing;

contributions on classic Web CMS modules (relational article model) and 
                            Structured CMS
                         modules;

evolving maintenance of classic Web CMS modules: relational model of articles/static
                                    content, with columns containing HTML fragments managed by marketing teams, and
                                    other columns locating content placement in website pages…;

content types (without HTML) are defined by a JSON schema, content being edited
                                            with a schema-driven
                                                editor;

management of translations/integration with Design/Marketing teams and front-end development: Bootstrap, 
                            Devextreme
                         and jQuery frameworks;

study of the “custom element centric” Lit framework: promoted
                            by Google, offering a vision of future web applications based on standardized multi-vendor
                            web-component ecosystems rather than relying on a single framework/vendor;

integration of the Python ERP Odoo and YII
                                 development of a PIM
                                 integrated with the ERP;

assistant IT director role on the IS roadmap (macro project planning…) and part-time
                                    product owner role collaborating with seven departments to align ERP integration
                                    with business processes;
